\fs62 \cf2 \cb3 Task 1: Create an Amazon RDS Instance\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs50 \cf2 \cb3 In this task, you create an Amazon RDS database for MySQL.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\fs58 \cf2 \cb3 Access the RDS console\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa100\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\fs50 \cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
At the top of the AWS Management Console, in the search bar, search for and choose 
\f1 \cf5 Aurora and RDS
\f0 \cf2 .\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\fs58 \cf2 \cb3 Create your database\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\fs50 \cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
In the left navigation pane, choose Databases.\cb1 \
\ls3\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Choose 
\fs47\fsmilli23600 \cb6 Create database
\fs50 \cb3 .\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\fs58 \cf2 \cb3 Configure database settings\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa100\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\fs50 \cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	6	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
In the Engine options section, configure the following:\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa100\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0\cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
For Engine type, choose MySQL.\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0\cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	7	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
In the Templates section, choose Dev/Test.\cb1 \
\ls6\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	8	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
In the Availability and durability section, select Single-AZ DB instance deployment (1 instance).\cb1 \
\ls6\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	9	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
In the Settings section, configure the following:\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa100\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0\cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
For DB instance identifier, enter 
\f1 \cf5 cloudage
\f0 \cf2 .\cb1 \
\ls7\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
For Master username, enter 
\f1 \cf5 engineer
\f0 \cf2 .\cb1 \
\ls7\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Under the Credentials management section, choose the Self managed option.\cb1 \
\ls7\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
For Master password, paste the P@ssw0rd value from the left side of these lab instructions.\cb1 \
\ls7\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
For Confirm master password, paste the P@ssw0rd value from the left side of these lab instructions.\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa100\partightenfactor0
\ls8\ilvl0\cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	10	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
In the Instance configuration section, configure the following:\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa100\partightenfactor0
\ls9\ilvl0\cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
For DB instance class, choose Burstable classes (includes t classes).\cb1 \
\ls9\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
From the dropdown menu, select the db.t3.micro instance type.\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa100\partightenfactor0
\ls10\ilvl0\cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	11	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
In the Connectivity section, configure the following:\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa100\partightenfactor0
\ls11\ilvl0\cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
For Virtual private cloud (VPC), select Lab VPC.\cb1 \
\ls11\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
For VPC security group (firewall), select Choose existing.\cb1 \
\ls11\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
For Existing VPC security groups, select RDS Security Group.\cb1 \
\ls11\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Remove the default security group from the Existing VPC security groups field by selecting the X next to it.\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\ls12\ilvl0\cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	12	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Expand the Additional configuration main section at the end of the page.\cb1 \
\ls12\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	13	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
In the Database options section, configure the following:\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa100\partightenfactor0
\ls13\ilvl0\cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
For Initial database name, enter 
\f1 \cf5 staging
\f0 \cf2 .\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\ls14\ilvl0\cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	14	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
In the Backup section, unselect Enable automated backups.\cb1 \
\ls14\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	15	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
In the Maintenance section, unselect Enable auto minor version upgrade.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\fs58 \cf2 \cb3 Launch the database instance\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\ls15\ilvl0
\fs50 \cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	16	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Choose 
\fs47\fsmilli23600 \cb6 Create database
\fs50 \cb3 .\cb1 \
\ls15\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	17	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
On the Suggested add-ons for cloudage pop-up window, choose 
\fs47\fsmilli23600 \cb6 Close
\fs50 \cb3 .\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 The RDS console displays a message like \cf3 \cb7 Successfully created database cloudage\cf2 \cb3  on top of the screen.\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\ls16\ilvl0\cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	18	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Monitor the RDS console until database Status shows Available.\cb1 \uc0\u8232 \cb3 Note: Database creation takes approximately 5-10 minutes.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\fs58 \cf2 \cb3 Locate your RDS endpoint\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\ls17\ilvl0
\fs50 \cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	19	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Choose cloudage link to view the database details.\cb1 \
\ls17\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	20	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
In the Connectivity & security section, copy the Endpoint.\cb1 \uc0\u8232 \cb3 The endpoint looks similar to: cloudage.crwxbgqad61a.region.rds.amazonaws.com\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 Task complete: You have successfully created an Amazon RDS database instance.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\fs62 \cf2 \cb3 Task 2: Connect to your RDS database from EC2\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs50 \cf2 \cb3 In this task, you establish a secure connection to your Amazon RDS database from your EC2 instance using AWS Systems Manager Session Manager.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\fs58 \cf2 \cb3 Connect to your EC2 instance\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\ls18\ilvl0
\fs50 \cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	21	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
In a new browser tab, paste the CommandHostSessionUrl value from the left pane of these instructions.\cb1 \uc0\u8232 \cb3 This opens a terminal session to your EC2 instance.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\fs58 \cf2 \cb3 Connect to your RDS database\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\ls19\ilvl0
\fs50 \cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	22	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Command: In the Session Manager terminal, enter the following command:\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
